<title>GERMANY: Early 1997 EU butter stocks put at 80,000 T.</title>
<headline>Early 1997 EU butter stocks put at 80,000 T.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union butter stocks were at 80,000 tonnes in early 1997, up 10,000 tonnes from a year earlier, a German farm ministry report detailing dairy sector statistics said on Monday.</p>
<p>Out of the total, German stocks amounted to 6,000 tonnes versus 5,000 tonnes a year earlier, the ministry said.</p>
<p>German butter production in 1996 was down by 1.2 percent from 1995 at 480,300 tonnes.</p>
<p>Low-fat milk powder stocks totalled 123,000 tonnes in the EU in early January, sharply higher than 14,000 tonnes a year earlier, the report said.</p>
<p>Some 21,000 tonnes of the total were in Germany, against nil the year before.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
